In contrast, in-vehicle mobile phone tasks include a large typology such as texting,

2 conversing, navigating, and answering, among many others. Until now, the focus has mainly

3 been on the conversation task; however, activities like conversing require the execution of other

4 supporting tasks including dialling, answering, monitoring the battery and reaching for the

5 phone. Research in this area must be able to consider these elements to provide a more realistic

6 representation of the extent of MPDD. Another interesting opportunity for research is to

7 understand the effects of ringing, navigation and dialling tasks.

